# Test: fn let-softening macro is triggered when another macro outputs
# a Call(fn, ...) AST node with non-LetDecl params.
# The wrap-fn macro generates a Call to fn using the legacy dict format;
# the fn macro normalizes the params (Call(x,[y]) → proper Fn params).
# The fn/class/type macros are globally registered via prelude.llt; no include needed.

[macro wrap-fn [let params body]
  [
    type:       "call"
    implied:    false
    fn:         [type: "var"  name: "fn"]
    args:       [0: params  1: body]
    named-args: []]]

[add-fn: [wrap-fn [x y] [+ x y]]]
[add-fn 3 4]
=== error
[E002] undefined variable: fn (did you mean the string "fn"? Use quotes.) (defined at 1:1-1:1) (called at 15:1-15:13)
  in [add-fn ...] at 15:1-15:13
